Doing fairly well (easily the farthest I've gotten in the game on my
current run, given that I just got back into it after not playing in
about 5 years), dungeon stomped Kojiro the samurai down about 12
levels of the main dungeon, then climbed back up to deal with the
Gnomish Mines.  Had a decent amount of stuff, was going well.

I probably should have gotten worried when I got set upon by four
nymphs on Level 5 and they didn't steal anything but my food.  All of
my food.  One of them went as far as to SEDUCE ME TO STEAL A
EUCALYPTIS LEAF.  I managed to get an edible corpse from a gnome,
descended to Level 6, started wandering around and accidentally popped
a watchman because I forgot that pressing up and left at the same time
results in a "y" command being sent to the program.  Wasn't thinking,
killed him because he was hitting me.  The others start coming at me. 
Immediately fled back upstairs.  Wandered for a little bit trying to
gain a level so I could maybe have that extra bit of strength to kill
all the watchmen since it looked like that was what was going to have
to happen.  As I'm returning to the stairs, Kojiro gets hungry.  No
corpses to eat, so I keep going.  By the time I reach the stairs, it's
pretty dire.  My immediate worry was food, so I was going to make a
mad dash for the store and hope there were some gunyoki in there.

No dice, says the RNG.

Kojiro faints while going down the stairs.  He is immediately set upon
by three watchmen and a watch captain, and as he has fainted and thus
can't react at all, all I see is this string of messages rushing by
faster than I can read, the extent of which I don't even know because
THERE'S MORE THAN 60 SO THEY START GETTING SCROLLED OUT, ending with
the ubiquitous DYWYPI.

Stupid nymphs.  Stupid, stupid nymphs.

